310d57de (2178 1792694297139 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f318") (src . "relation: a selector's field clause takes a wildcard, and refuses a variable\n\nAn endpoint selector written as (field decision _) was accepted at\ndeclaration and then matched nothing: every link under the relation was\nrefused relation-endpoint, whether the end was created in the same batch or\ncommitted before. Now `_` in a field clause holds for any value the block\ncarries for that field (a contested field, answering none, does not hold),\nas the query language reads it, and a value that is neither a literal\n(string, exact integer, symbol) nor `_` -- a variable included -- is refused\nat declaration, selector-value-not-literal, on every write route. The\nrefusal lives in the write path only: a declaration an earlier build\naccepted keeps its old reading on replay and survives a snapshot round trip.\nAn old declaration written with `_` now holds for any value; nothing stored\nis reinterpreted, since no edge could have been written under it before.\ntest/rule-check.sc grows ten rows (the wildcard, the missing field, the\nliteral control, the variable on each route, the replay and the snapshot);\nthe README's relation paragraph says the wildcard and the boundary.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 453))))
